# Own-wording Wizard traditions of Valda's Spire of Secrets, 2014 rules. Stratagem and spell tables come from the source.
SUB = {
"Familiar Master": {"spab": "Intelligence",
 "f": {
  "Arcane Evolution": "As an action, spend a spell slot to transform your familiar. Choose a beast with CR no higher than half the slot's level. Your familiar takes its appearance and statistics but keeps its creature type, and it can attack on its turn. This lasts 10 minutes, after which you pick its form from those the find familiar spell allows.",
  "Improved Familiar": "You always have find familiar prepared and it does not count against spells prepared. You can cast it as an action with no material components. When choosing your familiar's type, you can also pick aberration, construct, elemental or undead.",
  "Servitor's Gift": "While you have a familiar, you gain a benefit from its current form, even after Arcane Evolution. Bat: as a bonus action gain blindsight 15 ft while not Deafened. Cat: when you land from a jump or fall, use your reaction to reduce falling damage to 0. Crab: unarmored AC equals 12 + your Dexterity modifier. Frog: jump distances triple. Hawk: Advantage on sight-based Wisdom (Perception) checks. Lizard: Resistance to Poison damage. Octopus: while grappled, use a bonus action to try to escape, and add your Intelligence modifier (minimum +1) to the Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check. Owl: Darkvision 30 ft. Poisonous Snake: extra 1d4 Poison damage on a melee weapon hit. Quipper: swim speed 30 ft and double breath holding. Rat: Advantage on saves against poison and disease. Raven: add your Proficiency Bonus to death saves and know spare the dying, using Intelligence, not counted against cantrips known. Sea Horse: add your Proficiency Bonus to checks to control a mount and count as one size smaller for choosing mounts. Spider: climb speed 30 ft. Weasel: squeezing costs no extra movement and you stand from Prone for 5 ft of movement.",
  "Empower Familiar": "As a bonus action, give your familiar temporary hit points equal to twice your wizard level. You can also change its creature type and its form from the find familiar list. Short or Long Rest to use again.",
  "Servitor's Greater Gift": "While you have a familiar, you gain a benefit from its creature type. Aberration: you can change a damage spell's type to Psychic, and you have Resistance to Psychic. Celestial: when you spend a spell slot to cast a spell or use Arcane Evolution, a creature within 30 ft regains hit points equal to your Intelligence modifier + the slot level, and you have Resistance to Radiant. Construct: nonmagical critical hits against you become normal hits and you gain +1 AC. Elemental: you can change a damage spell's type to acid, cold, fire, lightning or thunder, and you speak, read and write Primordial. Fey: when you spend a spell slot to cast or use Arcane Evolution, you can teleport 5 ft x the slot level, and you have Advantage on saves against Charm and Frightened. Fiend: when you spend a slot to cast or use Arcane Evolution, a creature within 30 ft takes cold, fire or necrotic damage of your choice equal to your Intelligence modifier + slot level, and you have Resistance to Fire. Undead: you can change a damage spell's type to Necrotic and you have Resistance to Necrotic."},
 "acts": {"Arcane Evolution": "action", "Empower Familiar": "bonus"},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Empower Familiar", "lvl": 10, "max": 1, "reset": "short", "tag": "Familiar gains temp HP, may change type"}]},

"Magic Missile Mage": {"spab": "Intelligence",
 "f": {
  "Force Missile": "You learn magic missile if you do not know it. When you cast it: you fire 1 extra dart (2 at level 6, 3 at level 10, 4 at level 14). Your missiles bypass effects such as shield that block or reflect magic missile. You can cast it at its lowest level with no spell slot a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier, regaining all on a Long Rest. From level 14 this is unlimited.",
  "Shield of Missiles": "You can cast magic missile into a tight orbit around you for up to 10 minutes. You gain AC equal to the number of orbiting missiles, starting at the number fired, up to +6. When a hostile creature ends its turn within 5 ft, one missile hits it for normal damage and leaves the orbit. When you cast magic missile you can add some or all orbiting missiles to the spell. Short or Long Rest to use again.",
  "Counter-Missile": "When you see a creature within 60 ft cast a spell, use your reaction to cast magic missile with every missile aimed at it. It makes one Constitution save against the total damage to keep concentration while casting, even if the spell needs no concentration. If it fails, the spell fails.",
  "Inescapable Missile": "The range becomes 500 ft. You can target creatures you cannot see in range if you hear them and a path exists in range from you to them. Your magic missile cannot be countered by counterspell. Your missiles pass through constructs of magical force, such as wall of force, Leomund's tiny hut and Otiluke's resilient sphere."},
 "acts": {"Counter-Missile": "reaction"},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Force Missile", "lvl": 2, "max": "mod:INT", "reset": "long", "tag": "Free lowest-level magic missile"},
        {"feature": "Shield of Missiles", "lvl": 6, "max": 1, "reset": "short", "tag": "Orbiting missiles, +AC up to 6"}]},

"Mystic Savant": {"spab": "Intelligence",
 "f": {
  "Arcane Strategist": "You use stratagems fueled by battle dice. You have two d6 battle dice. Using one expends it. You regain all on a Short or Long Rest or when you roll initiative. The die size and number rise at certain levels, per the table. Once per turn you can expend a die to use a stratagem. You learn three stratagems and two more at level 6, then one more each at levels 10 and 14. When you learn new ones you can swap one you know. You can use only one stratagem per spell.",
  "Bonus Proficiency": "You gain proficiency in one skill of your choice: Arcana, History, Insight, Investigation, Medicine, Nature, Perception or Religion.",
  "Stratagems": "Arcane Warding: when you cast a spell of 1st level or higher, expend a die as a bonus action to gain temporary hit points equal to the slot level + the roll, lost after 10 minutes. Eldritch Aegis: when you or a creature you see within 30 ft takes spell damage, use your reaction to reduce it by the roll. Flash of Brilliance: add a die to an Intelligence or Wisdom check, even after the roll but before the result is announced. Mystic Counsel: as a bonus action, advise a creature within 30 ft that hears you. Once in the next minute it can add the die roll to a save against a spell. Mystic Defense: as a reaction, add a die to your save against a spell or magical effect, after the roll but before the result is announced. Potent Casting: when you roll spell damage, expend a die as a bonus action to reroll up to your Intelligence modifier (minimum 1) of the damage dice and keep the new rolls. Precision Spell: as a bonus action, add a die to a spell attack roll, before or after rolling but before effects apply. Quick Thinking: add a die to your initiative roll, after rolling but before order is set. Sorcerous Spread: when you damage a creature with a spell of 1st level or higher, use a bonus action and a die to choose another creature within 5 ft of the target. It takes damage equal to the slot level + the roll, of the same type. Spellcaster's Sting: when a creature you see within 60 ft passes a save against your spell of 1st level or higher, use a bonus action and a die. It takes Force damage equal to the slot level + the roll. Spell Sundering: when you damage a creature concentrating on a spell, use a bonus action and a die to add the roll to the damage. Its concentration save from that damage has Disadvantage. Unbreakable Concentration: add a die to a concentration save, after the roll but before the result is announced.",
  "Versatile Memory": "As an action, swap one prepared spell for another of the same level or lower from your spellbook. Short or Long Rest to use again.",
  "Arcanist's Assessment": "As an action, appraise the spellcasting of a creature you see within 30 ft. Make a check with your spellcasting ability against its spellcasting ability check (a d20 if it has none). On a success you learn whether it has Spellcasting, Innate Spellcasting or Pact Magic, and whether it can cast spells above your highest level. It knows you assessed it regardless. You cannot use this on the same target for 24 hours. You can use it a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum 1) and regain all on a Long Rest.",
  "Font of Percipience": "As a bonus action, spend a spell slot to regain expended battle dice up to the slot's level. You can also swap one stratagem you know."},
 "acts": {"Versatile Memory": "action", "Arcanist's Assessment": "action", "Font of Percipience": "bonus"},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Versatile Memory", "lvl": 6, "max": 1, "reset": "short", "tag": "Swap a prepared spell"},
        {"feature": "Arcanist's Assessment", "lvl": 10, "max": "mod:INT", "reset": "long", "tag": "Appraise a creature's spellcasting"}],
 "fx": [[2, "Bonus Proficiency", {"notes": [["Note", "Bonus Proficiency: one skill of your choice from Arcana, History, Insight, Investigation, Medicine, Nature, Perception, Religion"]]}]]},

"School of Chronomancy": {"spab": "Intelligence",
 "f": {
  "Chronomancy Savant": "All spells with the chronomancy tag are added to the wizard spell list for you. Copying a spell into your spellbook takes 10 minutes per spell level.",
  "Chronoshift": "When you cast a spell of 1st level or higher with a casting time of 1 action, you can spend another slot of the same level to make it 1 bonus action for that casting. You can do this a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum 1) and regain all on a Long Rest.",
  "Speed of Thought": "As an action, enter a state of focus that lets you do purely intellectual tasks, such as research, translation or computation, five times faster while you concentrate as on a spell. You must be able to do the task alone, and others cannot meaningfully help. Casting a spell, performing a ritual or moving more than 10 ft from where you began returns you to normal time at once, and you are faint and cannot maintain concentration for 1 minute.",
  "Lag Spell": "When you cast a spell, you can delay its effect by one, two or three turns. You choose the target and the delay when you cast, and roll any attack rolls then. Other effects, including saves, resolve when the spell triggers at the start of your turn after the delay. If conditions change so the spell becomes impossible, such as the target leaving range, it fails. Short or Long Rest to use again.",
  "Foreimage": "When you finish a Long Rest, you begin a second attempt at the day, followed by a temporal shadow that repeats your first run. Acting on your foreknowledge destroys the shadow until your next Long Rest and gives one benefit. Advantage on an attack roll, ability check or saving throw. Or one attack roll without Advantage misses you. Or you act on one thing you could have learned before the day's end, such as a riddle answer, a pit trap's place, a labyrinth's path or a name. Once used, all remaining foreknowledge is lost until your next Long Rest."},
 "acts": {"Speed of Thought": "action"},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Chronoshift", "lvl": 2, "max": "mod:INT", "reset": "long", "tag": "Cast an action spell as a bonus action"},
        {"feature": "Lag Spell", "lvl": 10, "max": 1, "reset": "short", "tag": "Delay a spell 1 to 3 turns"},
        {"feature": "Foreimage", "lvl": 14, "max": 1, "reset": "long", "tag": "Use foreknowledge once per day"}]},

"School of Gastronomy": {"spab": "Intelligence",
 "f": {
  "Monster Dish": "When you finish a Short or Long Rest, you can prepare a meal from a monster you and your allies slew. It uses the whole corpse, which died within 24 hours or was kept by gentle repose. It cannot be a celestial, humanoid or undead. The meal feeds a number of creatures equal to your Intelligence modifier and spoils after 24 hours. A creature eating it at the end of a Short or Long Rest rolls d6s equal to the ingredient's challenge rating (1d6 for CR 1/2 or lower) and gains that many temporary hit points. If the creature had immunity to a damage type other than Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing, you can make the meal give Resistance to one such type for 8 hours. You can prepare one meal, and regain this on a Long Rest.",
  "Sous Chef": "You gain proficiency with cook's utensils and have Advantage on ability checks to cook or prepare ingredients. You can cast create food and water once with no spell slot, regaining it on a Long Rest. The food it makes is a mouthwatering meal of your choice.",
  "Flavor Blast": "Once per turn, when a creature fails a save against your spell of 1st level or higher, you can make it smell and taste like delicious food for up to 1 minute or until you use this again. The odor reaches 15 ft and can be any food you choose. While it lasts, bite and teeth attacks against the target have Advantage, and it has Disadvantage on Constitution saves to keep concentration. Creatures of Intelligence 3 or lower cannot tell the target from the smell. Most creatures can tell after dealing damage to it.",
  "Bottomless Feast": "You can cast heroes' feast once for one creature, with no spell slot or material components. At level 11 it feeds 5 creatures. Long Rest to use again.",
  "Ravenous Magic Mouth": "As an action, summon a Large mouth of magical force with sharp teeth in an unoccupied space you see within 60 ft. On each of your turns you can move it up to 30 ft with no action, and use a bonus action to make it bite a creature within 5 ft. It uses your spell attack bonus. On a hit it deals 4d10 Force damage and grapples the target (escape DC your spell save DC). It grapples one target at a time and attacks only that creature. If it grapples a Medium or smaller target at the start of your turn, use a bonus action to make it swallow the target into an acid-filled extradimensional space. The swallowed creature is Blinded and Restrained and takes 4d6 Acid damage at the start of each of its turns. It can use its action to make a Strength save against your spell save DC. On a success it reappears Prone in an unoccupied space within 5 ft of the mouth. It escapes automatically when the mouth vanishes. The mouth lasts 1 minute or until you dismiss it on your turn. Long Rest to use again."},
 "acts": {"Ravenous Magic Mouth": "action"},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Monster Dish", "lvl": 2, "max": 1, "reset": "long", "tag": "One monster meal per Long Rest"},
        {"feature": "Sous Chef", "lvl": 2, "max": 1, "reset": "long", "tag": "Cast create food and water free"},
        {"feature": "Bottomless Feast", "lvl": 10, "max": 1, "reset": "long", "tag": "Cast heroes' feast free"},
        {"feature": "Ravenous Magic Mouth", "lvl": 14, "max": 1, "reset": "long", "tag": "Summon a biting mouth, 4d10 Force"}],
 "fx": [[2, "Sous Chef", {"notes": [["Note", "Sous Chef: proficient with cook's utensils. Advantage on checks to cook or prepare ingredients"]]}]]},

"School of Somnomancy": {"spab": "Intelligence",
 "f": {
  "Deep Sleep": "You add sleep to your spellbook if it is not there. When you cast it: the total hit points affected equal double the dice result. The radius is 30 ft. You choose the order in which creatures are affected.",
  "Somnambulist": "While you sleep you can move around freely, navigating from memory since you do not fully perceive your surroundings. You can copy spells into your spellbook while asleep.",
  "Mesmerize": "By repeating an action for 1 minute, you can hypnotize a willing creature within 60 ft that sees and hears you. While hypnotized it is semi-conscious and Charmed by you. Other spells and effects that charm or influence its mind have no effect, and you can have it repeat its save against such effects, ending them on a success. It recalls its memories perfectly, even altered or suppressed ones, and truthfully answers any question you ask. You can plant a single command word in its subconscious for up to 24 hours. The first time it hears the word while not hypnotized, it performs the one action or says the phrase you set, even against a compulsion from a spell. It stays hypnotized for up to 1 hour, until it takes damage, or until you end it with a special word.",
  "Dreamspeaker": "You add dream to your spellbook if it is not there. When you cast it, the messenger can jump among up to 12 creatures, each saving separately, talking with any of them. It can appear monstrous to only one target, and the spell then ends at once.",
  "Fitful Slumber": "At the start of the turn of any creature under a sleep spell you cast, you can have it take 3d6 Psychic damage. This cannot wake it or reduce it below 1 hit point."},
 "acts": {"Mesmerize": "special"},
 "fx": [[2, "Somnambulist", {"notes": [["Note", "Somnambulist: you can move and copy spells into your spellbook while asleep"]]}]]},
}
